sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Three published findings connect potassium channels to fin size in zebrafish and to fin proportion in flying fishes, and each was verified against its PubMed abstract: kcnk5b gain of function enlarges fins, longfin overexpresses kcnh2a, and Daane 2021 implicates lat4a with kcnh2a in flying-fish fin proportion" ;
    dct:description "Status: supported (by the cited abstracts, each quoted verbatim; no new experiment). (1) Gain-of-function mutations in the potassium channel kcnk5b (the 'another longfin' mutant) give proportionally enlarged fins in zebrafish. Quote: \"alf mutants carry gain-of-function mutations in kcnk5b\" (PMID 24453984, doi 10.1371/journal.pgen.1004080, Perathoner S 2014, PLoS Genet). (2) The classic longfin (t2) mutant is a regulatory kcnh2a allele that overexpresses this potassium channel and elongates the fins. Quote: \"longfint2 chromosome 2 overexpresses the ether-a-go-go-related voltage-gated potassium channel kcnh2a\" (PMID 34061172, doi 10.1242/dev.199384, Stewart S 2021, Development). (3) A phylogenomic study of flying fishes found signatures of convergent paired-fin enlargement and, intersected with zebrafish fin-size mutants, implicated lat4a and kcnh2a. Quote: \"we identify a surprising role for an L-type amino acid transporter, lat4a, and the potassium channel, kcnh2a, in the regulation of fin proportion\" (PMID 34534441, doi 10.1016/j.cub.2021.08.054, Daane JM 2021, Curr Biol). The symbol lat4a is ZFIN's slc43a2a on three records: human SLC43A2 is aliased LAT4 (NCBI Gene 124935); ZFIN curated PMID 34534441 itself to slc43a2a, allele dmh26, with decreased fin length; and the paper's own Data S1 sheet G lists lat4a under medaka Ensembl id ENSORLG00000009715, which Ensembl names SLC43A2, with a convergent F326L substitution in both gliding halfbeaks and at least 7 of 9 flying-fish species. Wording: fin enlargement for gliding, never a fin-to-wing transition. What it does not establish: No measurement in a flying-fish fin; the flying-fish result is phylogenomic association plus zebrafish genetics. It does not show that these genes alone set flying-fish fin size, nor any flying-fish ortholog identity. Pre-registration: none: a literature verification of leads named in the thread brief, not a hypothesis test." ;
    delphi:context "PubMed queries run: \"kcnk5b AND fin\" (6); \"another longfin zebrafish\" (28); \"longfin AND kcnh2a\" (2); \"flying fish AND fin AND (bioelectric OR potassium)\" (1); \"Exocoetidae AND fin\" (4). Abstracts in genotype/cache/pubmed_abstracts.xml. In the map, kcnk5b is the only sufficient-for link at the organ layer; kcnh2a is not attached to any node because ZFIN records no single-gene kcnh2a fish for the longfin allele." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "PubMed abstracts and ZFIN rows behind the three fin-size leads" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/map.vetted.json fin_size.verified_leads and genotype/cache/pubmed.json." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Verbatim quote check: each quoted sentence is asserted to be a substring of the fetched abstract (genotype/build.py cite()). No statistical test." ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/pubmed-eutils-fin-size-searches>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/ncbi-gene-slc43a2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/zfin-bulk-downloads-2026-10-31> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:map ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "supported (by the cited abstracts, each quoted verbatim; no new experiment)" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_leads_verified" ; schema:value "4"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "leads with a quote from a fetched abstract" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-fin-size-potassium-channel-leads-verified> schema:additionalProperty sub:m2 .
  sub:m2 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "n_zfin_fin_size_genes" ; schema:value "220"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "zebrafish genes with any ZFIN fin size or length phenotype, any allele type, GOF and LOF not separated" .
